Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

/*****************************************************************************
    jitSlotT3 -- BATCH ONE OF THE SWEEP. 2026-08-17.

    The four remaining comparisons migrate together: >=, <, <=, ==. With > from
    op two, that is the whole ordered half of the jitCmp family on slots.

    THE ASSERTION IS A COUNT OF FOUR -- one per migrated op in this action, and
    exactly the batch size. That is the batch discipline: a batch of N asserts
    the slot count moving by N, so an op that silently failed to install would
    show as N-1 rather than hiding behind three siblings that worked.

    ⚠ THIS ACTION CONTAINS NO ARITHMETIC, ON PURPOSE. The obvious way to fold
    four comparisons into one asserted value is to add them up -- but plus is
    itself a sweep candidate, so the day it migrates this rung's expected count
    would silently become seven and somebody would "fix" the target. An
    assertion that moves for reasons unrelated to what it certifies is noise
    (H3). Four ifs assigning distinct constants keep this number pinned to the
    four ops it is about, permanently.

    ⚠ AND THE VALUE STILL DEPENDS ON THE COMPARISONS, which is what stops the
    count from being the only live row. Each fire lands on a different constant
    because a different comparison was the last one true:

        fire 1, 6 and 3:  >= true -> 1, < false, <= false, == false   => 1
        fire 2, 3 and 6:  >= false, < true -> 2, <= true -> 3, == false => 3

    1 and 3 differ, so a folded constant cannot satisfy both, and NEITHER is
    zero -- a row a do-nothing default could also produce asserts nothing.

    H7 SPOT CONTROL for this batch, measured 2026-08-17 by pulling ONE member's
    registration -- the <= entry -- from incant setup, which is read at run time
    so no rebuild is involved:

        all four registered   slot count 4    fire 1 = 1   fire 2 = 3
        <= pulled             slot count 3    fire 1 = 1   fire 2 = 3

    ⚠ THE VALUES DO NOT MOVE. Only the count does. That is the whole reason this
    campaign asserts counts: the migration is value-transparent by construction,
    so the products cannot see it and a rung built on them would certify nothing.

    ⚠ OUTPUT FIELD INITIALIZED BEFORE THE FIRE (bear-trap 26 -- an uninitialized
    field reads back as its own tag). JITTED HALF FIRST (bear-trap 25). ONE
    testing call then jitRefire, never two.
*****************************************************************************/

register(JitLadder);
define
    jsbA;
    jsbB;
    jsbOut;
    jsbAll code={
        jsbOut = 0;
        if jsbA >= jsbB;    jsbOut = 1;
        if jsbA < jsbB;     jsbOut = 2;
        if jsbA <= jsbB;    jsbOut = 3;
        if jsbA == jsbB;    jsbOut = 4;
        };
    ;

jsbA = 6; jsbB = 3; jsbOut = 0;
print "JSB fire 1 setup : jsbA =" jsbA " jsbB =" jsbB:;
testing(jsbAll);
print "JSB fire 1 result: jsbOut =" jsbOut " (want 1)":;

jsbA = 3; jsbB = 6; jsbOut = 0;
print "JSB fire 2 setup : jsbA =" jsbA " jsbB =" jsbB " (recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();
print "JSB fire 2 result: jsbOut =" jsbOut " (want 3)":;

jsbA = 6; jsbB = 3; jsbOut = 0;
jsbAll();
print "JSB interpreted  : jsbOut =" jsbOut " (the oracle -- want 1)":;
print "JITSLOT3 SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
